  "body_markdown": "About us\n\nmeet Dr. ChrisMeet The TeamLivewell DifferenceOffice TourTechnologyJoin Our Team\n\nservices\n\ndCOEFull Mouth ReconstructionSedation Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nSmile MakeoverPorcelain VeneersNo Prep VeneersGum RecontouringTeeth WhiteningDental Bonding\n\nImplant Dentistry\n\nDental ImplantsSingle ImplantsImplant BridgesAll-on-X ImplantsLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nDental CrownsInlays & OnlaysDental BridgesTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone GraftingRidge AugmentationTooth ExtractionSinus LiftWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nOrthodontics\n\nInvisalignBraces\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPreventive DentistryPreventive CleaningGum TherapyRoot Canal Therapy\n\nTMJ TreatmentDental Emergencies\n\nnew patient\n\nfirst visit & new examInsurance & FinancingBlog\n\nOur work\n\nSmile GalleryTestimonials\n\nContact\n\ncall (703) 690-0102Request An Appointment\n\nBook Now\n\n703-690-0102\n\nLivewell Difference\n\nmeet Dr. Chris\n\nMeet The Team\n\nJoin Our Team\n\nOffice Tour\n\nTechnology\n\nServices\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nDCOE\n\nTMJ Treatment\n\nDental Emergencies\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPreventive\n\nDental Bridges\n\nRoot Canal\n\nProfessional Dental Cleaning\n\nScaling & Root Planing\n\nAll General Dentistry services\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nNo Prep Veneers\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nGum Recontouring\n\nAll Cosmetic Dentistry Services\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Bridges\n\nAll-on-X Implants\n\nLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nAll Implant Dentistry Services\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nTooth Extraction\n\nSinus Lift\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nInvisalign\n\nBraces\n\nAll Orthodontics Services\n\nDental Crowns\n\nTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nDental Bonding\n\nInlays & Onlays\n\nAll Restorative Dentistry Services\n\nNew Patient\n\nfirst visit & new exam\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nBlog\n\nTestimonials\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nCALL US: (703) 690-0102\n\nBOOK AN APPOINTMENT\n\n320+\n\n5 Star Reviews\n\n\n# General Dentistryat Livewell Dental\n\n\nRoot cause focus, not just routine repair\n\nComprehensive care, one doctor start to finish\n\nMost patients never need emergency treatment\n\n\n## Most Dentists Tell You What's Wrong. We Tell You Why It Keeps Happening.\n\n\nA cavity isn't just a cavity. It's a sign that something in your oral environment - bacteria levels, bite forces, diet, or hygiene habits - is working against your teeth. Most offices fix the cavity and send you home. We ask what created it in the first place.\n\nThat question changes everything about how we practice general dentistry. We track your data at every visit, test your bacterial load when the pattern suggests we should, and build a care plan around your specific risk profile - not a generic six-month protocol.\n\nOne patient at a time - no double-booking, no rushed appointments\n\nData tracked at every visit and compared against your last\n\nTreatment recommendations grounded in evidence, not habit\n\nSame doctor manages everything from your cleaning to your crown\n\nStart With a Full Evaluation\n\n\n## The Mouth You Have at 60 Is Built by the Decisions Made Today\n\n\nLearn About Our Approach\n\nMost dental problems are preventable. The ones that aren't are almost always detectable early - when the solution is simple, fast, and inexpensive. The patients who end up needing the most complex treatment are rarely the ones who were unlucky. They're the ones whose warning signs weren't caught, or weren't explained.\n\nAt Livewell, we tell you exactly where you stand at every visit. Not vague reassurance - actual numbers, actual comparisons, actual risk assessment. So you can make informed decisions about your own health.\n\n\n## Find the Right Solution for Your Situation\n\n\n\n### Preventive Care\n\n\nPrevention isn't just cleaning your teeth twice a year. It's tracking bacterial load, measuring gum health at every visit, and matching your care intensity to your actual risk level. The goal is a mouth that stays healthy between appointments, not one that resets every six months.\n\nExplore Preventive Care\n\n\n### Dental Bridges\n\n\nWhen a tooth is missing, a bridge fills the gap by spanning from one supporting structure to another. We offer three types - tooth-supported, implant-supported, and Maryland bridges - because the right choice depends on your specific situation, not what's easiest to place.\n\nExplore Dental Bridges\n\n\n### Root Canal Treatment\n\n\nA root canal removes infected tissue from inside a tooth and seals it to stop the spread of damage. Done well, it saves a tooth that would otherwise need to be extracted. Done at Livewell, it's precise, comfortable, and built to last.\n\nExplore Explore Root Canal Treatment\n\n\n### Dental Emergencies\n\n\nA broken tooth, severe pain, a lost restoration, or a dental abscess - when something can't wait, we make room for you. We also spend time understanding what caused the emergency so the same problem doesn't repeat itself.\n\nExplore Emergency Dentistry\n\n\n### Professional Cleaning\n\n\nWe use EMS Airflow - a warm water and powder system that removes biofilm more thoroughly than traditional scaling, with less abrasion and less sensitivity. It reaches below the gumline and around implant surfaces where standard instruments can't. Not the same cleaning you've had before.\n\nExplore Professional Cleaning\n\n\n## How We Work Through Every Case\n\n\nNot All General Dentistry Is the Same - and That Matters More Than You Think\n\nWe Start With the Full Picture\n\nYour first visit includes a comprehensive clinical exam, digital X-rays, intraoral scan, and a full review of your dental and medical history. We're not looking for what to bill - we're building an accurate picture of your oral health so every recommendation that follows is grounded in real data.\n\nWe Tell You What We Found and Why It Matters\n\nAfter the exam, Dr. Chris walks you through the findings in plain language. What's stable, what's at risk, what needs treatment now, and what can wait. You leave the first visit knowing exactly where you stand - not just that you have \"a few small cavities.\"\n\nWe Build a Plan Around Your Priorities\n\nSome patients want everything addressed immediately. Others need to phase treatment over time. We work around your schedule, your budget, and your comfort level - without compromising on what actually needs to happen for your long-term health.\n\nTreatment Is Done With Precision, Not Speed\n\nDr. Chris works under magnification on every procedure. Rubber dam isolation is used for every bonding case. We don't rush through appointments because we don't double-book. One patient at a time means the work gets done right the first time.\n\nWe Track, Compare, and Adjust Over Time\n\nAt every recall visit, we compare your current data against previous visits - gum measurements, bacterial levels, X-ray changes. If something is trending in the wrong direction, we catch it early. If everything is holding steady, we tell you that too.\n\n\n## One Doctor. Your Entire Journey.\n\n\nAt most general dentistry offices, you see whoever is available. Your history lives in a chart that may or may not be reviewed before your appointment. The person who placed your filling isn't the one who monitors it three years later.\n\nAt Livewell, Dr. Chris is the only dentist. He knows your case because he built it. Every exam, every treatment, every follow-up appointment - the same person, with the same standards, every time.\n\nFellow, Academy of General Dentistry (FAGD) - top 6% of general dentists nationally\n\nGraduate, Kois Center - evidence-based diagnosis and treatment planning\n\nAEGD, UCSF - advanced training beyond dental school\n\n10+ years in practice, 1,300+ patients treated\n\n\n## The Technology Behind General Dentistry at Livewell\n\n\nSee All Our Technology\n\n\n### EMS Airflow\n\n\nNot a standard cleaning. A more thorough one.\n\nA warm water and powder spray removes biofilm, staining, and deposits more completely than metal scalers - without the abrasion or sensitivity. It reaches subgingival areas and implant surfaces that traditional instruments can't access safely.\n\n\n### OralDNA Salivary Testing\n\n\nGum disease has a cause. This is how we find it.\n\nA saliva sample identifies the specific bacteria driving periodontal risk - and at what levels. That information turns a generic treatment protocol into a targeted one. Different bacteria require different responses.\n\n\n### Intraoral Scanning\n\n\nDigital records that improve every time we use them.\n\nA 3D scan of your teeth and bite creates a precise digital model used for treatment planning, restoration design, and baseline comparison at future visits. No trays, no impression material.\n\n\n### CBCT 3D Imaging\n\n\nWhen a flat X-ray isn't enough, we go three-dimensional.\n\nFor complex diagnoses, bone evaluation, or cases where anatomy affects the plan, CBCT gives us a full 3D model of your bone, roots, and jaw structure. Used selectively, when the case warrants it.\n\n\n### High-Powered Loupes\n\n\nEvery procedure done under magnification. Every time.\n\nDr. Chris works under magnification on every patient, every appointment, without exception. Margins, cracks, and early decay that are invisible to the naked eye become detectable and manageable.\n\n\n## What Patients Say About Their Results\n\n\nSTORIES OF THE LIVES WE’VE TOUCHED\n\nWhat does general dentistry include?\n\nGeneral dentistry covers the full range of care most patients need - preventive cleanings and exams, fillings, bridges, root canals, emergency treatment, and ongoing health monitoring. At Livewell, it also includes salivary bacterial testing, comprehensive risk assessment, and data tracking across every visit.\n\nHow often should I see a general dentist?\n\nTwice a year is the standard recommendation. At Livewell, the frequency depends on your actual risk level. Low-risk patients may maintain well on two visits per year. Patients with active gum disease or elevated bacterial risk may need more frequent monitoring. We tell you what your data suggests, not what the calendar says.\n\nWhat if I haven't been to the dentist in several years?\n\nCome in. We see patients who haven't had care in two years, five years, or longer - without judgment. We assess where things stand, tell you what's urgent, what can be phased, and what the path forward looks like. The goal is to get you stable and keep you that way.\n\n\n### Common Questions About General Dentistry\n\n\nContact Us\n\n\n### Reimagine your dental experience\n\n\n\n### address\n\n\n9027 Silverbrook Rd Ste. F\n\nFairfax Station, VA 22039\n\n\n### Contact\n\n\n\n### Hours\n\n\nMon-Tue: 8am-5pm\n\nWed-Thu: 8am-4pm\n\nFri: 8am-1pm\n\n\n### Connect\n\n\nServing Fairfax Station and the Greater Northern Virginia Area\n\nCopyright © TEXT-YEAR Livewell Dental\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms of Service\n\nCookie Policy\n\nHIPAA Disclosure\n\nConsent Preferences",
